{{! How the heat (how often each place was visited) is drawn, as JSON (its drawing, activities-map-heat.js, reads it): a smooth glow
    (Leaflet.heat), from `low` (a place visited once) through to `high` (the busiest), on a log scale; `min_opacity` is how
    faint the faintest heat is, `radius_cells` how far each cell's heat spreads, in cells.  The size of cell is chosen for the
    zoom (about 100 m, 870 m or 7 km), so the glow looks much the same at every zoom; zoomed in so far that it would be more than
    60 pixels, what Leaflet.heat can draw, the heat is not drawn (the routes say more there). }}
{
  "low": "#ffd43b", "high": "{{{red}}}", "min_opacity": 0.3, "radius_cells": 1.5
}
